Joaquin, there was no real question: there's one sensible way to keep the pool whole. The agent should have just done it, and I shouldn't have passed it on to you. One agent now owns the rest of the generation:
- it builds that pool's 3 TeV block from smaller runs of the same integration, checked against its complete runs first;
- it collects the last 12 pools when their workers finish;
- it runs the final check over all 113.

I also caught a slip of my own. Recording your answer on the plan replaced the generation entry's later steps instead of adding to it. That dropped two of them: the pp validation and the pure-default pretraining pair that follows it. I've restored both, waiting on the rebuild. That's the plan tool's `answer --set next` overwriting every next step, and I'll make it add rather than replace.
